WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
Good Morning Hank, it's Tuesday!

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.240
I'm Maureen Johnson filling in for John Green because once again,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.260
he has contributed to the birth of a human child.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.780
This is really nerve-wrecking for me, because I'm a writer, like John,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.680
but like, I don't make videos all the time,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.440
and, y'know, I don't think I'm really good at it.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.840
So, y'know, I got my camera, I got my watermelon

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.760
(chews)

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.400
Today's topic is:

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.280
The INTERNET!

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.740
Yeah, the internet, the whole thing.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.760
Some people don't like the internet.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.700
And it can be for a number of reasons.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.320
For example, there are people like my Mom,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.620
who gets confused by the internet and generally doesn't know how it works

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.800
and is constantly afraid she's going to break it.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.880
[Maureen's "Mom":] Maureen? Maureen, Maureen!

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.860
The people that hate or dismiss the internet often say things

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.760
like "Well, back when I was a kid, you know, we didn't just sit around

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.260
and watch porn all the time and make animated JIFF-ies!"

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.280
Yeah, that may be true, but you probably also didn't

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.320
engage in a political discussion with a thousand people, so - shut up!

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.120
I'm not saying the level of discourse is always high,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.540
I mean, I filled in for John when he went on maternity leave the first time,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.580
And on my first video, 90 % of the comments just said:

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.900
Oh mah God, John has Bewbs!!1!

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.100
Sometimes we are gonna get breaking news from the middle of the seat of government,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.080
and sometimes we are gonna have:

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.740
[slurring voice]: I just really love cats ... and...[sniffles]

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.560
I want them to be...[sniffle] ... on a rainbow...

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.660
The last 4 weeks have been pretty fraught

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.300
and there's been a lot going on in the media, and the world

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.180
that is kinda hard to talk about.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.380
It makes us both want to talk -

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.640
ALL the time, and not know how to talk at all.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.380
There's a lot of...split opinions.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.300
It's hard to sort of know what to say to people who are

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.160
of a different viewpoint than you.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.340
Without screaming, or ripping out your hair,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.580
or just go nuts and turn into some kind of crazy Troll

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:53.100
just going around the internet, going, "Troll Troll Troll Troll, I just wanna watch the world burn!"

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.860
And that is not productive.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.240
Bu it doesn't mean we can't talk about these things that are difficult

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.140
where our opinions differ wildly

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.440
in fact, we HAVE to talk about these things. And I think in many ways,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.480
the Internet is teaching us how to talk to each other.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.760
In a big way, in a big way that we've never done before.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.040
and we are just learning the language of mass discussion.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.840
But it's easy to say we can use the internet to talk about things,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.560
we all know it's actually really difficult. That's why, you know,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.740
the one rule of the internet is: "Don't read the comments!!"

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.660
But Okay. Too late. You've read the comments,

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.000
it's already done, what do you do now?

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.700
Pause. Breathe! Look at some cats!

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.020
And ask yourself:

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.860
What do you want to accomplish?

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.680
Do you want to further a good cause that you are already part of,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.660
or do you want to punch a Troll in the face?

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.960
And you probably want to...

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.560
...do both of those things.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.020
But you're probably only going to to be able to accomplish one of them.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.320
And you probably shouldn't be so focused on one.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.160
Does it improve the situation, or the cause, or whatever it is your trying to promote

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.280
or encourage, or talk about?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.480
Or just punch a Troll in the face?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.900
And the answer, unfortunately, is "probably not".

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.440
It doesn't make your side look good,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.840
it doesn't further the discussion,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.880
so therefore, sadly, a lot of time you're not going to

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.960
be able to make that comment into a teachable moment!

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.100
What am I even talking about?

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.860
Just - GO for it. Just answer ALL the Trolls. Do it. NOW!

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.800
Troll Patrol starts now! Let's do this thing!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.060
Honestly, start here. Start on this video, start looking in the comments,

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.660
and be like, "UR DUMB" - "NO, UR Dumb". - "BOOBS!"

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.180
No one knows how to "internet". If anybody tells you they know how to internet,

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.120
Just go tell them to go eat some watermelon,

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.760
because that's the only thing that makes sense in this mixed up world of ours.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.340
I don't know what you people want from me.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.380
Just follow me on Twitter or something, I dunno.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:45.060
[mumbling] I'm good at Twitter. I'm good at Twitter, I'm not...

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.560
...I'm not great at videos.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:50.960
I'm very, very good at Twitter, though.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.320
go there.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.780
[unintelligible, squeaking, high-pitched]

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.120
[high-pitched]: I'm sorry

